(l) Amendment in Rule 2 of the Rules of Procedure.- that in the Rules of Procedure andConduct of Business in the National Assembly,2007, in Rule 2.-(l) in the definition of "Minister", the expression "or a Parliamentary Secr€t:rry inrespect ofany function delegated or entrusted to him by a Minister", shall be omitted.
(2)
(2) after the definition of"Parliament House", the following new definition, shall beinserted, namely.-"Parliamentary Secretary" refers to a member appointed in respect c,f anyparliamentary functions assigned, delegated, or entrusted exclusively by the Ministerof the Ministry or Division to which the Parliamentary Secretary is appointed."Insertion of new Rules in the Rules of Procedure.- that in the Rules of Procedure and
Conduct ofBusiness in the National Assembly, 2007, after rule 398, the following news rules shallbe inserted, namely.-
(3)
"39C. The Cabinet shall collectively be responsible to the National Assembly, in accordancewith Clause (6) ofArticle 9l ofthe Constitution ofthe Islamic Republic of Pakistan.39D. The Minister shall assume primary responsibility for the disposal of businesspertaining to his or her portfolio.39E. In cases of emergency, and with the prior approval ofthe Speaker, the ParliamentarySecretary may be allowed to assume the parliamentary functions of the Minister ofthe respective Ministry or Division, subject to prior intimation to the NationalAssembly Secretariat".Amendment in Rule 247 of the Rules of Procedure.- that in the Rules of Procedure and
Conduct ofBusiness in the National Assembly, 2007, in Rule 247, in sub-rule (3), for the full stop acolon shall be substituted and thereafter the following proviso shall be added at the end namell:-"Provided that the notice of a Parliamentary Secretary shall only lapse in respect of theministry or division to which the Parliamentary Secretary is appointed."13. SYED RAFITILLAH to move under sub-rule (5) of rule 293 of the Rules of Procedure andConduct of Business in the National Assembly, 2007, that the proposed amendments be taken intoconsideration.14, SYED RAFIULLAH to move that the proposed amendments in the Rules of hocedure andConduct of Business in the National Assembly, 2007. be adopted.
PRESENTATION OF PERIODICAL
RT OF IHE STAN'DING COMMITTtrE
15. SYED ABDUL QADIR GILAI\-I, Chairman Standing Committee on Planning, Development andSpecial Initiatives to present the Periodical Report ofthe Committee for the period lst July, 2024 to 3lstDecember, 2024, as required by rule 234-A of the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in theNational Assembly, 2007.RESOLUTIONS16. SYED RAFIULLAII to move the following resolution:-"This House is of the opinion that the Govemment should take immediate steps to provide inexpensi,re andspeedy justice to the citizen across the country."17. MS. SHARMILA SAIIIBA FARUQUI HASHAAM to move the following resolution:-"This House is of the opinion that the Govemment should take immediate steps to reduce the electricitytariffs to facilitate the textile sector."
18. MR. JAM ABDIIL KARIM BIJAR to move the following resolution:-"This House is ofthe opinion that the Government should take immediate steps to regularize the servjces ol-daily wager teachers who are working under the federal govemment schools and colleges.,'
