MOTIONS T]NDER RULE 25921. MS. SHARMILA SAHIBA FARUQUI HASHAAM to move the following motion:-"This House may discuss the deportation of Pakistanis from different countries.22, MR. AI\IJUM AQEEL KIIAN to move the following motion:-"This House may discuss the quality of services provided in Federal Govemment Hospitals for patients."23. SYED RAFIULLAH to move the following motion:-"This House may discuss the situation arising out of increase in the prices ofelectricity in the country."24. MS. ALIYA KAMRAN to move the following motion:-"This House may discuss the performance ofCapital Development Authority.
DISCUSSION ON A MATTER OF URGENT PUBLIC IMPORTAIICE UNDER RULE 87
25. MS. ALIYA KAMRAN to discuss a matter of urgent public importanceregarding discontinuation oftax exemption to teachers and researchers, equal to 25o/o of tax payable on theirincome from salaries, same was previously allowed in terms of Income Tax Ordinance, 2001.MATTERS OTHER THAI\I POINTS OF ORDER
26.
Raising matters under Rule l8 which are not Points ofOrder.CALLING ATTENTION NOTICE
27. MS.ALIYAKAMRAN MR. MUHAMMAD USMAN BADIM to inviteaftention of the Minister for Federal Education and Professional Training to a matter of urgent publicimportance regarding severe financial difficulties being faced by public sector universities, causing graveconcern amongst the public.
Islamabad, thel Tth February, 2025
TAHIR HUSSAINSecretary General
3
19. MR. ASIF KHAN to move the following resolution:-"This House is ofthe opinion that the Govemment should take immediate steps to provide uninterruptedelectricity to residents of NA-32, Peshawar-V (Khyber Pakhtunkhwa)."20, MS, ALIYA KAMRAN to move the following resolution:-"This House is of the opinion that the Government should take immediate steps to reduce the fees ofmedical colleges working under Pakistan Medical and Dental Council (PMDC)."

